      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T20:28:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: I wonder if this is a potential foot-gun (violating single-responsibility-principle and sometimes doing **two** operations: reset + allocate).  Not sure if my vague feeling can be made actionable somehow:\n\n* Document the `reset` in the doc comment?\n* `SkASSERT_RELEASE` that there is no pre-allocated buffer?  In other words - force user to explicitly call `reset(...)` + `allocateFromBudget(...)` themselves?\n* Other options?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 383,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 383,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "7329a7f2a71dc26cfc4c5dcddf576e8c0b1d389e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30d0e3ab_be8dfc4e",
        "filename": "src/codec/SkCodecPriv.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 383,
      "author": {
        "id": 4772438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T23:29:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this a very good point: considering it’s a `BudgetedBuffer` we certainly don’t want users of this class to get confused when calling `allocateFromBudget` twice. Charging the budget twice in this case seems rather counter intuitive, and an explicit `reset` call would make that much clearer.\n\nI went with your assert + explicit reset option, thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "4698cfed_b8092e87",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 383,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 383,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "7329a7f2a71dc26cfc4c5dcddf576e8c0b1d389e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28d78659_1bbdd6da",
        "filename": "src/codec/SkCodecPriv.h",
