        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T20:28:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we have a `static_assert` that the new container class is ` contiguous_range`?  Inspiration comes from https://github.com/dtolnay/cxx/blob/b2971717da380618ea8ab5a3bf9ee68434e1f684/src/cxx.cc#L499-L504 (I landed a PR to make `rust::Slice` a contigous range, originally those static asserts were in `cxx.h`).\n\nAI says that once `contiguous_range` holds, `std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e{buf}` constructs directly from our container (if it\u0027s also sized), and generic code can rely on `std::ranges::data` and `std::ranges::size`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 418,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 418,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "7329a7f2a71dc26cfc4c5dcddf576e8c0b1d389e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
